# {{ project_name }}

Generated by `codegraph init` from a .mox model (rexlang) — JSON Schema
interop via `import schema "path/to/schema.json" as Name` in your .mox files,
or `codegraph migrate --schemas <dir> --output <dir>` to convert a JSON
Schema directory to .mox.

## Quickstart

```sh
just generate   # ingest the .mox model + generate into generated/
just api        # API integration tests (postgres + hurl + curl smoke + RLS)
just e2e        # end-to-end: supabase -> generate -> migrate -> build -> playwright
just classify   # show entity/VO classification decisions
just doctor     # validate project layout and configuration
```

Prerequisites: just, cargo, psql, hurl (api suite), and for e2e: Docker with
the Supabase CLI, pnpm, and Playwright chromium.

## Layout

```
model/                mox model files, one per domain (the primary model source)
domains.toml          domain configuration
profiles.toml         generator profiles and feature flags
codegraph-ops.toml    ops harness configuration (testkit, ports, db targets)
hurl/                 hurl contract tests
{{ graph_binary }}/   codegen wrapper binary (run/classify/generate/doctor)
crates/domain-types/  generated-into domain types crate
crates/hooks-api/     generated-into hooks API crate
ops/testkit/          ops harness test runner crate
generated/            generated application code (gitignored)
```

## Codegraph pinning

The workspace pins codegraph crates to git rev `{{ codegraph_rev }}` in
`Cargo.toml`. During codegraph development, re-run init with
`--codegraph-path` to switch the workspace to local path dependencies.

## Modeling contract: optionality and ref naming

- **Features are required by default.** A plain feature (`date due_date`)
  demands a value in every create payload; declare the `[0..1]` multiplicity
  (`date[0..1] due_date`) for an optional (`Option`) field. The models in
  `model/` use plain features everywhere — widen with `[0..1]` when a field
  should not be mandatory.
- **Ref fields have one name per relation.** A scalar `refers` arrives and is
  accepted as `x_id: Uuid`; an array `refers` (junction) is accepted as
  `x: [Uuid]` — and also as `x_id` (a serde alias, so the scalar spelling
  works there too). Request and response DTOs use the same name.
- **Wrong field names are rejected, never ignored.** Create/update DTOs
  carry `#[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]`: a misspelled or near-miss field
  fails with a 422 whose message names the accepted spellings, so a link can
  never silently land as NULL.

See <https://github.com/magick93/codegraph> for the generator project.
